Generated from the OCaml tree on the Mac by lib/flow_shader print_shader (via dune build) from lib/ogpu_metal/shaders/present.rays.
present.metal is the presentation blit (Ogpu_metal.Presentation) the Rust ogpu_metal crate embeds until the Rust flow_shader port exists; that port must reproduce it byte for byte (golden test).
conformance/*.metal are the MSL sources of lib/ogpu/conformance/conformance.ml (the Metal side of the OGPU conformance suite), dumped by running that file with its shader picker writing each shader out.
rt_extra.metal is the working-tree (barycentric) conformance.ml's, with `triangle_data` added to the motion/instancing intersector tags: Metal's intersection_result carries no triangle_barycentric_coord without it, so the uncommitted conformance.ml's rt_extra does not compile on Metal as written. flat_*.metal/argument_fragment.metal/textured_fragment.metal come from the committed (HEAD) conformance.ml (the working-tree run stopped at that compile error before reaching the render shaders; they are unchanged by its diff).
